Revision history for App-Actions - run GitHub Actions workflows locally

0.002.0
	- The test that walks t/fixtures now checks each example against its
	  schema as it reads it, so a fixture with the wrong shape is named
	  and rejected there, like one that is not valid JSON, and does not
	  count towards the schema coverage check.
	- make check-staged and make check-worktree now list each check they
	  ran, as passed (with its test count) or failed, and each they skipped,
	  so a clean run shows that the live-knob check ran rather than only
	  that nothing failed.  A commit that passes the hook is still silent.
	- t/regex.t's time limits are scaled up when Devel::Cover is loaded.
	  The CI coverage job runs the suite under it, which made the
	  40,000-comparison tokenizer case (linear, but about five times
	  slower there) fail its two-second limit.
	- Documented the configuration that Object::Configure adds to
	  App::Actions->new and action-run: an App__Actions section in the
	  Config::Abstraction files (base/local in CONFIG_DIR or ~/.conf) and
	  App__Actions__* environment variables, both of which win over the
	  arguments and the command line and are not validated.
	- Warnings and errors from a run (a failed step, a job that could not
	  run, a container or log that could not be kept) now go through a
	  Log::Abstraction logger, at the error or warn level.  By default it
	  prints them to standard error as before.  App::Actions->new takes a
	  logger argument: a Log::Abstraction object, an array to collect the
	  messages in, a hash of Log::Abstraction options, or 'NULL' to turn
	  them off.  A logger in an App__Actions (or UNIVERSAL) configuration
	  section replaces the default; the argument replaces both.  Progress
	  lines, command echoes and the summary stay on standard output.
	- Log::Abstraction 0.41 is now required directly.  It sets
	  Sub::Private's mode for its own package only, so t/error.t's TODO now
	  applies only to an older Log::Abstraction.
	- The tests set CONFIG_DIR to an empty directory, so a developer's own
	  ~/.conf files (such as a UNIVERSAL logger) cannot change what they see.
	- Added t/function.t, white-box tests of every routine in lib/.  They
	  found the bugs below.
	- Security: an environment value is now interpolated once.  Before,
	  ${{ }} text that came from a context value (a commit message, say)
	  was evaluated again, which could show a secret, and each further
	  reference could double the work.  A variable that refers to itself,
	  directly or through others, is now an error
	  (runner.env_cycle).  The new App::Actions::Runner::Support::Env does
	  the lookups.
	- Security: keep_logs refuses a log name or run id that is not a plain
	  file name (runner.logs.bad_name), so it cannot write outside the log
	  directory.
	- Expression is re-entrant: a call made while another is being
	  evaluated (for example from a context lookup) no longer corrupts it,
	  and nothing from a call is kept in the object.  Booleans interpolate
	  as true and false; an array index out of range is missing; negative
	  numbers are read; a quoted }} does not end an expression; format()
	  replaces each placeholder once.
	- Action: a true word is matched to the end of the string (\z), so
	  "true\n" is not true.
	- Workflow: each matrix instance gets its own copy of the job, so
	  changing one no longer changes the others.
	- Cache: load() drops pulls and last_used entries of the wrong shape;
	  base_directory() handles an empty HOME.
	- Check: run() puts the output handle back when a check dies; an
	  object's os is used by host_info().
	- Process: a child's output is flushed before it runs the program;
	  run_parallel truncates each output file once and every program then
	  appends to it; run() takes an append option.
	- Schema: JSON booleans compare by their truth.
	- Error and I18N: an argument whose value is undef is dropped before
	  validating, so a required one is reported as missing; named pairs
	  given to a routine with positional names are accepted.
	- Parallel: jobs are still collected when waitpid returns -1 (as it
	  does with $SIG{CHLD} = 'IGNORE'); a job's prints go to its own log;
	  a cut log name no longer ends in a separator.
	- Images: a pull with no result counts as failed.
	- Containers: container options or service entrypoints with a quote
	  that is not closed are an error (runner.options_invalid) rather than
	  being run as nothing; a host name made from a job name no longer
	  starts or ends with - or .
	- Steps: a condition that cannot be evaluated fails the step; a docker
	  action's args with a quote that is not closed are an error
	  (runner.docker_action.bad_args); INPUT_ names keep - and ., as
	  GitHub's do, and Docker now hides such names in the environment.
	- Runner: a matrix instance with continue-on-error does not stop the
	  others under fail-fast, as on GitHub; a container user given by the
	  current user's name is not treated as a different user.
	- App::Actions: a workflow in /.github/workflows has / as its project
	  directory, not the current directory.
	- t/space-path.t is skipped when AUTOMATED_TESTING is set, unless
	  SPACE_PATH is true: under Devel::Cover its second run of the suite took
	  most of an hour of the dashboard job.
	- The cache and logs listings (their headings, column names and
	  "just now" / "ago" ages) and the two lines a child process prints when
	  it cannot redirect its output or start its program now come from the
	  message catalogues, so they are in French, German or Chinese when that
	  language is chosen.  The English text is unchanged.  The JSON documents
	  are not translated.
	- New test dependencies: Test::Mockingbird 0.14, Test::Returns 0.05 and
	  Test::Memory::Cycle 1.06, for t/function.t.  Test::DescribeMe and
	  Test::Warn are no longer listed; no test used them directly.
	- Added t/changes.t, which checks the shape of this file: the newest
	  release is the modules' version, every release has items and a date
	  in date(1)'s form (only the newest, dated when it is released, may
	  have none), and versions and dates go one way.
	- META: the repository URL is https (GitHub no longer serves git://),
	  and keys the META spec does not define are gone.
	- Windows: a program that is not there is no longer handed to system(),
	  which retried it through cmd.exe.  That reported status 1 and
	  "is not recognized" instead of 255, and let cmd.exe read & and | in
	  the arguments as commands.  The program is now looked for first (the
	  current directory and PATH, with a PATHEXT extension added to a bare
	  name), and a missing one is status 255, as on other systems.
	- The pre-commit hook's report names each check's test file with / on
	  every platform (it showed t\schema.t on Windows).
	- Added t/unit.t, black-box tests of every public routine against what
	  its POD documents.  It keeps a ledger of every catalogue message and
	  every documented status and fails if any is never reached.  It found
	  the bugs below.
	- if: false, pre-if: false, post-if: false and fail-fast: false are
	  honoured on Perl 5.36 and later.  YAML::PP loads false as Perl's own
	  boolean, which reads as an empty string, and an empty condition
	  (or fail-fast value) was taken as true, so the job or step ran.
	- A docker:// action's image is interpolated once.  It was
	  interpolated again after the uses: value had been, so ${{ }} text
	  from a step output was evaluated, and docker://${{ env.EMPTY }} was
	  skipped as an unsupported remote action instead of being reported
	  as having no image name.
	- The preflight lists docker://image:${{ steps.x.outputs.tag }} as
	  deferred, as documented, instead of as the image "image:", and so
	  does a local action's path built from a value the job will have.
	- A workflow mistake found while a step or job runs (no image name,
	  a missing local action, nesting too deep, no node, an environment
	  value that does not evaluate) is reported without a Perl source
	  location, as the other run errors are.
	- The caller's $@ is kept by Util::load_yaml_mapping,
	  I18N::validate_args, I18N::new, Error::new, Expression's fromJSON,
	  Cache::load and save, Logs::prune, Runner::Support::resolve_env,
	  Runner::Report::keep_logs, Runner::Parallel::run, the public methods
	  of Runner::Images, Runner::Steps::run, and Runner::new, run and
	  preflight.
	- Invalid arguments are an App::Actions::Error with the code
	  actions.invalid_arguments (the text is unchanged), and Error::new's
	  own message no longer carries the validator's prefix or a location.
	- Process::exit_code is always between 0 and 255, as documented.
	- Expression: a.1 is "Expected a property name after dot", as
	  documented, and fromJSON()'s message no longer names JSON::PP's file
	  and line, even when the installed path has a space in it.
	- Cache::save reports a directory it cannot make, and a temporary file
	  it cannot create, as "cannot write a new cache file in 'DIR':
	  REASON", without the library's file and line.
	- Logs::prune counts a log it removed before a later one failed.
	- Runner::Report::keep_logs reports a log directory it cannot make as
	  runner.logs.copy_failed, rather than with File::Path's text.
	- Schema: invalid_exit can be imported, as the POD says.
	- Removed three messages no run could reach (runner.fault.image_unnamed,
	  runner.job.did_not_run, runner.job.no_result) and the code that would
	  have printed them.
	- Runner::Containers::name treats a job without a matrix_index as index
	  0 rather than warning about an undefined value.
	- POD: Runner::Steps->new documents share_files; Runner::Images'
	  pitfalls say the cache warning needs verbose; Access and I18N::message
	  document what they do with a routine already wrapped and an unknown
	  key.

0.001.0	Thu Oct 22 12:40:02 PM EDT 2026
	- First release
